{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1543591-renegade-con-oct-2024-upcoming-wod5e-books","id":1543591,"title":"Renegade-Con Oct. 2024: Upcoming WOD5E books","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-11T12:41:11-07:00","id":1543591,"title":"Renegade-Con Oct. 2024: Upcoming WOD5E books","content":"I just watched the livestream and for anyone who's interested, I'm presenting here the three new supplements that were announced.<br /> <br /> The tl;dr is that it feels like with Shattered Nation WOD5E is now heading in a different direction. Bringing back legacy-lore, undermining or reversing elements/themes set up by the corebooks and making it all about more character-options and adding (some) Loresheets.<br /> <br /> For V5 we got: In Memoriam<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No Escape from the Past\u2026<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve been dead longer than you were alive. You've witnessed the passing of every mortal from your first life\u2014through violence, disease, or the relentless march of time\u2014while you, undying, remain bound to this world. Your nights are haunted by the echoes of history, from the distant whispers of two centuries past to the cataclysmic World Wars and the rise of the modern era.<br /> <br /> Embrace the mantle of the noveaux elders, the ancillae who have seized power in the absence of the true elders, who\u2019ve now fallen or been beckoned away. Become a Kindred of 100, 150, or even 200 years. Detail your backstory and relive the formative trials and tribulations that forged you into the monster you are today. Command the night with the power of centuries behind you with In Memoriam for Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Features<ul><li>Dive into and take part in Kindred history through flashback with expanded Memoriam rules.</li> <li>Craft Ancilla Characters with enriched rules designed for advanced play.</li> <li>Consolidated and Streamlined Memoriam Rules featuring new variations and advanced rules for deeper character development.</li> <li>New Lore, Resources &amp; Plotlines surrounding 11 mortal eras and 8 pivotal Kindred events.</li> <li>Six New Loresheets that link characters to significant historical moments.</li> <li>Learn more about integrating Memoriam rules into your existing stories and how to tie your characters to older events</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>For H5, the new supplement is called: Apostates<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Find yourself a better job!<br /> <br /> Whether you once ran a Monster-X franchise, served in the Special Affairs Division, consulted for the shadowy Arcanum, temped at Re:Venge, or volunteered for the Society of St. Leopold, working with the Orgs means you\u2019ve seen it all \u2014 and then some. But when the grind ignites a Drive deep within, it\u2019s time to break free and seek a new path. Step into the shoes of the disillusioned and defiant ex-Org operatives.<br /> <br /> Apostates empowers players to repurpose the assets of their former employers \u2014 everything from classified intel to cutting-edge gear and clandestine networks. Play as these rogue agents or unleash them as unpredictable rivals in your Hunter: The Reckoning chronicle. Whether as allies or adversaries, the apostates and their former Orgs are bound to shake up your story.<br /> <br /> Features<ul><li>Org details written for players along with Loresheets in Hunter: The Reckoning for the first time!</li> <li>Includes many player options with new Perks for your Edges and new Advantages and Flaws!</li> <li>Storytelling advice for incorporating apostate characters into any Chronicle with a pre-written story to play through as apostates, and 2 Chronicle sketches to jumpstart your chronicles</li> <li>Organizations gain a new spotlight in your Chronicles including S.A.D., Project Twilight and the new Red Eye Community Watch.</li> <li>Players have ties to the Orgs and Storytellers may focus games on Orgs as adversaries or rivals that may hunt the Hunters</li> </ul>\u200b </div> </div> </div>I guess this is the closest H5 will get to &quot;But what if I want to play a hunter who works for a hunter-org?&quot;. But it feels like such a waste. Like how Shattered Nation is bringing back all this legacy-lore but somehow it's also still trying to cling to the idea that Garou know nothing about their history. Here you have a supplement that is all about hunters in a hunter-org but it has to jump through this hoop of clinging to the corebook's premise by having the hunter-org-hunter be an &quot;apostate&quot;, ie he has just decided to leave the hunter-org right before the game starts - but the character still has a lot of ties to the hunter-org.<br /> <br /> For W5 the supplement is called: Wyrmtide. There's no page for it yet, so I can't copy-paste the blurb but to summarize what was said on the stream: It's essentially an antagonist-book. And if I remember correctly, the Cult of Fenris wasn't mentioned. It's BSD, Fomori, Bane Spirits, agents of the Weaver and interestingly, it sounded like Pentex Subsidiaries are back as well. But they also emphasized that it offers advice on how to structure chronicles where you fight your enemies and <i>win</i>. Also, it comes with the usual: More Gifts, Rites, Merits, Flaws and Loresheets.<br /> <br /> I like this direction but if Shattered Nation is an example of what this new direction looks like... In Shattered Nation they brought back legacy-lore but then also butchered it (the last king of the Garou Nation Albrecht was portrayed as a cranky old man who would beat people with his walking-stick when he felt disrespected), the amount of new character-options wasn't extensive and a big problem with the Loresheets in that book was that they were about uninteresting characters. And the character-writing is one of the biggest issues in Shattered Nation. They were either boring or annoying. So I'm dreading what this might mean for a supplement like In Memoriam that delves into VtM-history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T10:19:34-07:00","id":1543691,"title":"","content":"If the Chulorviah aren't in a book entitled &quot;Wyrmtide&quot;, then something has gone very wrong.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(I fully expect something to have gone very wrong.)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}